        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.846,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5 0 ^ { \\circ } ;"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " therefore, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 3 0 ^ { \\circ } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , because "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " form a linear pair, and linear pairs always add up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.125,
            0.846,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "∠2 and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are corresponding angles, and they need to be equal since lines l and m are parallel."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.162,
            0.318,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 3 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.18,
            0.624,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Angles "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "interior angles",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.229,
            0.826,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is there a relation between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 6 7"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " You could try to find the relationship by taking different values for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and see what "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is. Once you find a relation, try to justify it or prove that this relation holds always. You will find that the sum of the interior angles on the same side of the transversal always add up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.355,
            0.848,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In Fig. 5.29, line segment AB is parallel to CD and AD is parallel to BC. ∠DAC is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle  ADC"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What are the measures of angles "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle CAB , \\angle ABC,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and ∠BCD?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.418,
            0.847,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution: Let us observe the parallel lines AB and CD. AD is a transversal of these two lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.462,
            0.649,
            0.61
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.316,
                0.462,
                0.649,
                0.61
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 10,
              "bbox": [
                0.461,
                0.609,
                0.538,
                0.624
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 5.29"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.633,
            0.846,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that the sum of the interior angles formed by a transversal on a pair of parallel lines adds up to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 8 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . So"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.67,
            0.387,
            0.687
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle ADC+\\angle DAB=180^{\\circ}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.688,
            0.362,
            0.705
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "60^{\\circ} + \\angle  DAB  = 180^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.707,
            0.337,
            0.724
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{SO} \\angle \\mathrm{DAB} = 120^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.725,
            0.467,
            0.743
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm { C A B }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from this?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.744,
            0.402,
            0.761
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle DAB = \\angle DAC + \\angle CAB."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.762,
            0.39,
            0.779
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "120^{\\circ} = 65^{\\circ} + \\angle  CAB"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.78,
            0.325,
            0.797
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle CAB = 55^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.799,
            0.848,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us observe the parallel line segments AD and BC. They are intersected by a transversal CD. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{So}, \\angle \\mathrm{ADC}+\\angle \\mathrm{BCD}=180^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , because they are interior angles on the same side of the transversal. Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle  ADC"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is given as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 0 ^ { \\circ } , \\angle \\mathrm { B C D } = 1 2 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.872,
            0.474,
            0.889
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, we find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle ABC = 60^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.89,
            0.817,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, in Fig. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5.29,\\angle CAB = 55^{\\circ},\\angle ABC = 60^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle BCD = 120^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.938,
            0.192,
            0.954
          ],
